+## `[foil]` — only when `runtime.type = "foil"`
+
+Sandboxes are copy-on-write branches of a host folder, served by
+[`foil serve`](https://github.com/umbarsariya/foil/tree/main/integrations/opensandbox):
+no Docker, millisecond starts, Linux and macOS, and a sandbox's changes can
+be reviewed and applied to the real folder. `foil serve` runs execd's API in
+each sandbox; images are not used (`image.uri` is recorded only).
+
+| Key | Type | Default | Description |
+|-----|------|---------|-------------|
+| `url` | string | `"http://127.0.0.1:8090"` | Base URL of `foil serve`. |
+| `api_key` | string \| omitted | `null` | The key `foil serve` expects (its `OPEN_SANDBOX_API_KEY`). |
+| `api_key_env` | string | `"FOIL_SERVE_API_KEY"` | Environment variable read when `api_key` is unset. |
+| `workspace` | string \| omitted | `null` | Folder new sandboxes branch (one of `foil serve -w`); default: the first served. |
+| `endpoint_host` | string \| omitted | `null` | `host:port` clients use to reach `foil serve` directly, when not `url`'s. |
+| `timeout_seconds` | number | `60` | Timeout for calls to `foil serve`. |
+
+```toml
+[runtime]
+type = "foil"
+execd_image = "unused-by-foil"
+
+[foil]
+url = "http://127.0.0.1:8090"   # foil serve --listen 127.0.0.1:8090 -w ~/project --strict
+api_key_env = "FOIL_SERVE_API_KEY"
+```
+
+---
+
